# DocuMind AI — Engineering Rules

Senior AI engineer on an existing codebase. Small, measured, tested steps. Never rewrite
working systems for elegance.

## Preserve
Offline extractive mode; FAISS+BM25+RRF; filename+page citations; document-scoped
retrieval including cache keys; semantic cache; diagnostics; latency analytics; /health;
FastAPI/Streamlit; navy/teal UI.

## Rules
Read before changing. Config for thresholds. No API keys in code/logs/frontend. No agent
frameworks / React rewrite. Tests for every change — only claim pass if run this session.
Update CHANGELOG.md each phase. Commit each phase on its branch.

## Evaluation integrity
Never invent metrics. `label_source: human_verified` only after human check; agent drafts
are `draft`. Gold = (filename, page, span). Tune vs test split; tune thresholds only on
tune; headline numbers only on verified test. Results files include date, git commit,
config, corpus hash, split, counts, verified count. Ablations vs frozen baseline before
default-on.

## Out of scope unless asked
Auth, Postgres, PPTX, entity extraction, dedicated search page, React, pin/archive.

## Phase end
Stable commit + phase report; wait for user "continue" before next phase.
